{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27812,"name":"chioma christopher","username":"Kaylah","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/kaylah/{size}/11224_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-24T16:04:46.608Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi everyone \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/images/emoji/apple/waving_hand.png?v=15\" title=\":waving_hand:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":waving_hand:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e I’m Chioma, a builder in the CKBuilders program. I’ve been building \u003cstrong\u003eCrowns\u003c/strong\u003e, a real-time 3D car race where players put CKB on the line and the chain decides who won. It’s live on testnet, and I’d love for you to race it and tell me what you think.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlay:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://keepers-relay.vercel.app\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://keepers-relay.vercel.app\u003c/a\u003e (testnet)\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cstrong\u003eCode:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Kaylahray/keepers_relay\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - Kaylahray/keepers_relay: Crowns: live 3D car races on Nervos CKB. 2–5 players race 3 laps for a shared pot; each phone signs its own moves, and the chain replays the whole race before paying the winner. Rust rules on CKB-VM and in WebAssembly, Spore trophies, testnet. · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cstrong\u003eBuild thread:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Nervos-Community-Catalyst/CKBuilder-projects/issues/45\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCrowns: a live multiplayer skill game where CKB-VM replays every run · Issue #45 · Nervos-Community-Catalyst/CKBuilder-projects · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598_2_690x287.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"plhntnm85T63lI6wLbAh5VpkXJS\" width=\"690\" height=\"287\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598_2_690x287.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598_2_1035x430.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/b19e2a2ace5ed363e677ddf14c3ddd79ec040598.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"34261B\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1350×563 307 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956_2_690x326.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"qGc7Q0GzNmfS5VzOJfH8sULsEnk\" width=\"690\" height=\"326\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956_2_690x326.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/b/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956_2_1035x489.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/bafd9761c0496ef27e276b67b392b70987531956.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"141617\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1326×627 118 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/d/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e.png\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e_2_690x348.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"vIcSSFIZnky6u1MvhdvrHeVsVT8\" width=\"690\" height=\"348\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e_2_690x348.png, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e_2_1035x522.png 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/d/de42b120cb32ac71442c11aae56d39eb9f59b86e.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"282A1B\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1304×658 80.8 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-why-i-built-it-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-why-i-built-it-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhy I built it\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn most online games with money on them, you have to trust the server. It holds the money, it decides who won, and you can’t check either. I wanted a fast, real-time game where \u003cstrong\u003enobody\u003c/strong\u003e has to be trusted: not me, not the server. The chain holds the money and replays the race itself before it pays anyone.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-what-it-is-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-what-it-is-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat it is\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA race for 2 to 5 players: 3 laps, everyone driving at the same time, with items, boosts and crashes. Races come in two kinds:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEntry races:\u003c/strong\u003e everyone puts in the same entry fee in CKB, and the winner takes the whole pot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSponsored races:\u003c/strong\u003e the host puts up the prize and \u003cstrong\u003eyou join free\u003c/strong\u003e. You only lock a deposit for your seat, and it all comes back after the race.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the game:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3 tracks:\u003c/strong\u003e Harbour Loop (the fast one), Switchback Hill (tight hairpins) and Old Town (narrow streets), each with its own scenery.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e8 items\u003c/strong\u003e from pads on the road: Ram, Slick, Jolt, Barricade, Crown Rush, Ward, Patch and Draft. Crashes and hits cost health, and a wrecked car stops for a moment before it rejoins.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePhone or computer:\u003c/strong\u003e on a phone, touch the left or right side of the screen to steer, with buttons for boost and brake. On a computer, use the keyboard.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFree practice\u003c/strong\u003e against two bots on the same rules, with no wallet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTrophies:\u003c/strong\u003e win a race and claim a trophy, a Spore you own. You can only get one for a race you really won, and the CKB inside it stays yours.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProfiles:\u003c/strong\u003e claim an \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@username\u003c/span\u003e, which is a cell you own on chain. Upload a picture or pick a ready-made look, and it’s minted as a Spore you own and set as your profile picture. Your trophies, wins and crown shards show on your profile and on the leaderboard.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReplays:\u003c/strong\u003e anyone can open a finished race, see each driver’s time, shards and moves, and watch it again in 3D, rebuilt from the moves stored on chain.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-how-a-race-works-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-how-a-race-works-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow a race works\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHost:\u003c/strong\u003e someone opens a race and picks the track, the number of seats and when it starts (5 to 60 minutes). They either set an entry fee, or sponsor a prize and let players in free.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJoin:\u003c/strong\u003e players take a seat. Each player who joins takes a fifth off the time left.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStart:\u003c/strong\u003e when the clock reaches zero, everyone is taken into the race at the same moment, with a 10-second countdown.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePayout:\u003c/strong\u003e when the race ends, the winner is paid automatically. If nobody finishes, everyone gets their money back, and a sponsor gets their prize back.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour wallet only asks you once, when you join. While you race, your browser signs your moves with a temporary session key, so there are no popups mid-race.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-how-ckb-makes-it-fair-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-how-ckb-makes-it-fair-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow CKB makes it fair\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo one holds the money.\u003c/strong\u003e The host’s CKB sits in a match cell and each player’s in their own seat cell, all locked by the match script, \u003ccode\u003elive-match\u003c/code\u003e. Not me, not the server.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe chain is the referee.\u003c/strong\u003e The finish transaction carries every car’s moves. \u003ccode\u003elive-match\u003c/code\u003e \u003cstrong\u003espawns the game script\u003c/strong\u003e with \u003ccode\u003eckb-script-ipc\u003c/code\u003e and calls it like a function: \u003ccode\u003ejudge(record)\u003c/code\u003e replays the whole race tick by tick and returns each car’s place. Only then does \u003ccode\u003elive-match\u003c/code\u003e pay out.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNobody can fake a win.\u003c/strong\u003e Each player’s moves are signed by their own session key, and the script checks the winner’s signature. The race server (a small relay) passes moves between phones in real time, but it can’t invent them.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMoney can’t get stuck.\u003c/strong\u003e If the relay disappears, every entry can go back to its owner after a timeout the chain enforces, with nobody else’s signature.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSponsored races can’t be farmed.\u003c/strong\u003e Joining one needs a username cell in your wallet, which the chain checks through a cell dep, and the chain refuses one wallet taking two seats in a prize race.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOne set of rules everywhere.\u003c/strong\u003e The race rules are one Rust crate with integer maths only, compiled to RISC-V for CKB-VM and to WebAssembly for the browser and the relay, so all three always agree on who won.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAnyone can check it.\u003c/strong\u003e The results page reads the moves from the finish transaction, replays the race in your browser and checks it against who the chain paid.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-status-on-testnet-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-status-on-testnet-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eStatus on testnet\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003elive-match (type ID): \u003ccode\u003e0xcf2c00c07441a48baeb76284e8edb8d10c6e016865c3eb6b1f87ad3b57a146b7\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLatest upgrade, sponsored races (22 Nov): \u003ca href=\"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x4e13e90fccc84eed10f25a749daf0a14beb27566fd575ab66f292827d2b557d4\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e0x4e13e90f…57d4\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFirst sponsored race: a 100 CKB prize, and the winner got their deposit back plus the prize. \u003cstrong\u003e70,475,122 cycles\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href=\"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x8e3bca4466a106ec3196aa2aa9877262cd1f1c774c3215f12f5a69935b0af623\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e0x8e3bca44…f623\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA close entry race on 23 Nov: won by 1.5 seconds with 251 signed moves, and the whole race was replayed on chain before paying 200 CKB. \u003cstrong\u003e65,322,821 cycles\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href=\"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0xcef2e225ff74fc17a19020de74a58ba166324b3412f85f579a42a34c316ad515\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e0xcef2e225…d515\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e49 transaction tests in \u003ccode\u003eckb-testtool\u003c/code\u003e on the real RISC-V binaries, plus an OffCKB devnet test of seven full races with a real relay and bot drivers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe cycle counts above are the chain’s own. You can check them yourself: paste either hash into \u003ca href=\"https://ckb-cycle-tools.vercel.app/?tx=0xcef2e225ff74fc17a19020de74a58ba166324b3412f85f579a42a34c316ad515\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eckb-cycle-tools\u003c/a\u003e. It replays the finish in your browser and splits it per script: for the 23 Nov race, \u003ccode\u003elive-match\u003c/code\u003e and the game it spawns are 63.5M of the 65.3M (97.3%), and the replay matches the node’s total exactly. The worst case (5 cars, full 3 minutes, twistiest track) is about 141M in my tests.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-things-i-learned-on-ckb-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-things-i-learned-on-ckb-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThings I learned on CKB\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSpawn and IPC make a game a library.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003elive-match\u003c/code\u003e doesn’t know anything about racing. It only asks a game script “who won?”. Any game that serves the same trait could use the same match script and its money rules.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSame result everywhere needs integer maths.\u003c/strong\u003e One float anywhere and the phone and the chain would disagree. Fixed ticks and integer maths keep the browser, the relay and CKB-VM in step.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProfile the spawned script on its own.\u003c/strong\u003e In a spawn, the match script is the parent (VM 0) and the game is a child (VM 1), so a plain profile only sees the parent. With \u003ccode\u003eckb-debugger --vm-id 1\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/luongthanhtung03/ckb-cycle-tools\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eckb-cycle-tools\u003c/a\u003e, which can profile a spawned script on its own, I found that about half of the game’s cycles go to one function that finds the nearest point on the track. That’s where my next cut goes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA cell dep is a free check.\u003c/strong\u003e The sponsored-race username pass is read as a cell dep, so it costs the player nothing and the cell isn’t spent.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSigning live moves needs ordering.\u003c/strong\u003e I found that key presses sent as separate web requests could reach the relay out of order. The phone then refused to sign a list it didn’t recognise, and a winner could lose the prize. Now each phone has one WebSocket, and every press is numbered.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-what-it-doesnt-do-yet-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-what-it-doesnt-do-yet-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat it doesn’t do yet\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOne relay.\u003c/strong\u003e Only my relay runs races today. It can’t cheat, but if it’s down, races wait for the timeout refund.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReload mid-race:\u003c/strong\u003e a driver who reloads gets back into the race, but can’t sign the moves made before the reload yet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUsernames\u003c/strong\u003e are checked as free by the app before you claim one. Making that fully on chain is next.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLooks:\u003c/strong\u003e each car is just its seat’s colour. Car skins you own as Spores, richer environments and real car models are next.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27812-what-id-love-feedback-on-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27812-what-id-love-feedback-on-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat I’d love feedback on\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHow does racing feel on your phone? Is the steering responsive, and is the lag OK?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs anything confusing for someone new to CKB?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAbout half the replay is a nearest-point search on the track. Has anyone made a search like this cheaper in CKB-VM?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach phone signs its moves with a session key, and the chain checks only the winner’s signature before paying. Do you see a gap in that, or a more CKB-native way to do it?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt’s on \u003cstrong\u003etestnet\u003c/strong\u003e. Look for the gold \u003cstrong\u003eFree entry\u003c/strong\u003e races: you can join those without paying anything. Or grab some testnet CKB from the faucet and host your own, and share the link with friends: it shows a preview card of the race.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks for reading! \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/images/emoji/apple/chequered_flag.png?v=15\" title=\":chequered_flag:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":chequered_flag:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-24T16:04:46.608Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":24,"readers_count":23,"score":89.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":11367,"topic_slug":"crowns-a-live-3d-car-race-on-ckb-where-the-chain-is-the-referee","display_username":"chioma christopher","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://keepers-relay.vercel.app","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Crowns","clicks":5},{"url":"https://github.com/Nervos-Community-Catalyst/CKBuilder-projects/issues/45","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x4e13e90fccc84eed10f25a749daf0a14beb27566fd575ab66f292827d2b557d4","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0x8e3bca4466a106ec3196aa2aa9877262cd1f1c774c3215f12f5a69935b0af623","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"https://testnet.explorer.nervos.org/transaction/0xcef2e225ff74fc17a19020de74a58ba166324b3412f85f579a42a34c316ad515","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"https://ckb-cycle-tools.vercel.app/?tx=0xcef2e225ff74fc17a19020de74a58ba166324b3412f85f579a42a34c316ad515","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"ckb-cycle-tools","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/Kaylahray/keepers_relay","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - Kaylahray/keepers_relay: Crowns: live 3D car races on Nervos CKB. 2–5 players race 3 laps for a shared pot; each phone signs its own moves, and the chain replays the whole race before paying the winner. Rust rules on CKB-VM and in WebAssembly, Sp","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/luongthanhtung03/ckb-cycle-tools","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - luongthanhtung03/ckb-cycle-tools · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":5}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4267,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/crowns-a-live-3d-car-race-on-ckb-where-the-chain-is-the-referee/11367/1","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":5}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":5,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false,"can_translate":false},{"id":27815,"name":"Enzo","username":"cool007zqw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/cool007zqw/{size}/1679_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-25T02:53:01.769Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWell done.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe game is smooth on my phone though I only played in practice mode.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaybe add some bot player for the paid race?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-25T02:53:01.769Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":23.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":11367,"topic_slug":"crowns-a-live-3d-car-race-on-ckb-where-the-chain-is-the-referee","display_username":"Enzo","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Star Writer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1064,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/crowns-a-live-3d-car-race-on-ckb-where-the-chain-is-the-referee/11367/2","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":27829,"name":"chioma christopher","username":"Kaylah","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/kaylah/{size}/11224_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-25T16:37:31.196Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSorry for the late reply, and thanks for trying it! Glad it runs smoothly on your phone. \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/images/emoji/apple/raising_hands.png?v=15\" title=\":raising_hands:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":raising_hands:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve thought about bots for paid races. In a paid race, all the CKB comes from the players, so a bot racing for that money would need someone’s wallet behind it, and that someone would be me. I’d be betting against my own players, and I don’t want that. The whole idea of Crowns is that the chain is the referee and nobody has an edge, including me.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I might add later is bots that fill empty seats so a small race feels fuller. They’d be part of the game rules, so the chain drives them during its replay, but they’d never put in an entry or win the pot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor now, the way to try a real race without paying is a sponsored race, the host puts up the prize and you join free (look for the gold Free entry badge on the Races page). You just need a username.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m planning to host one soon. Would you join if I post the time here?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-25T16:39:45.394Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":16.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":11367,"topic_slug":"crowns-a-live-3d-car-race-on-ckb-where-the-chain-is-the-referee","display_username":"chioma christopher","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"fl